    "comments": [
      {
        "id": "comment-1",
        "text": "WHILE LOOP\n\nWhile Loop re-checks its Condition before every pass and runs Body while it is true.\nHere n starts at 1 and doubles until it reaches 100 or more: 1, 2, 4, 8, 16, 32, 64, 128.\nTake care: if nothing in the Body ever makes the Condition false the loop never ends. Pulsar runs one pass per frame (the loop is latent) so a stuck loop never freezes the game, but it will still run forever.",
        "position": [
          60.0,
          -300.0
        ],
        "size": [
          900.0,
          200.0
        ],
        "color": [
          0.2,
          0.4,
          0.8,
          0.3
        ],
        "contained_node_ids": []
      },
      {
        "id": "comment-2",
        "text": "CONDITION\nn < 100, recomputed from the variable on every pass. This wire is the loop's test.",
        "position": [
          60.0,
          680.0
        ],
        "size": [
          520.0,
          100.0
        ],
        "color": [
          0.2,
          0.65,
          0.35,
          0.3
        ],
        "contained_node_ids": [
          "gn",
          "below"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "comment-3",
        "text": "BODY\nDouble n, then count the pass. The condition is looked at again afterwards.",
